  "insights": [
    "The PRD reveals the project evolved from simple Vercel compatibility to a full split-stack architecture across three platforms",
    "Backend dependencies are carefully pinned with matching versions (pydantic/pydantic_core) to avoid compatibility issues",
    "The emergentintegrations library requires a private PyPI index, adding deployment complexity",
    "Frontend redesign explicitly removes AI/model branding while preserving prediction functionality",
    "The approved layout (Option A) prioritizes summary-first dashboard over city comparison or chart-forward approaches",
    "Implementation plan uses test-driven development starting with failing tests for pure helper functions",
    "Design spec defines 6 major UI sections with detailed requirements for each",
    "Test fixture covers multiple HTML parsing scenarios including edge cases and malformed data",
    "Security is enforced through URL validation and production error message sanitization",
    "The project follows live-data-only constraint, explicitly rejecting synthetic or interpolated values",
    "Scheduled captures at 14:00 and 21:00 Helsinki time provide twice-daily ground truth for accuracy tracking",
    "Backlog includes custom domain, monitoring, Redis caching, and premium alert features",
    "Monetization ideas center on threshold-based alerts and affiliate links to fuel apps",
    "The redesign maintains backward compatibility with existing backend API contract",
    "Finnish language UI is a hard requirement throughout all user-facing components"
  ]
}
